{{ if .RiskPolicySet }}
### Risk Matrix

Threat count by likelihood (rows) × impact (columns), shaded by the resulting
risk level. Worst case is top-right.

```{=html}
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Likelihood \ Impact</th>{{ range .RiskMatrix.Impacts }}<th>{{ . | upper }}</th>{{ end }}</tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{- range .RiskMatrix.Rows }}
<tr><th>{{ .Likelihood | upper }}</th>{{ range .Cells }}<td style="background:{{ riskColor .Level }};text-align:center">{{ if .Threats }}{{ len .Threats }}{{ end }}</td>{{ end }}</tr>
{{- end }}
</tbody>
</table>
```

```{=typst}
#align(center, table(
  columns: (auto,) * (1 + {{ len .RiskMatrix.Impacts }}),
  align: center + horizon,
  stroke: 0.5pt + gray,
  [*Likelihood*#linebreak()*Impact*], {{ range .RiskMatrix.Impacts }}[*{{ . | upper }}*], {{ end }}
{{ range .RiskMatrix.Rows }}  [*{{ .Likelihood | upper }}*], {{ range .Cells }}table.cell(fill: rgb("{{ riskColor .Level }}"))[{{ if .Threats }}{{ len .Threats }}{{ end }}], {{ end }}
{{ end }}))
```
